15 0 obj
<< /A 34 0 R /Alt (Schematic diagram illustrating the regulatory network of major immune checkpoints at the maternal-fetal interface. PD-1, CTLA-4, Tim-3, TIGIT, LAG-3, BTLA, and VISTA are shown with their respective ligands. Inhibitory interactions are marked with red circles containing a minus sign, stimulatory signals with green circles containing a plus sign, and dashed lines indicate stimulatory signaling pathways. The diagram highlights how these checkpoints coordinate to balance T cell, NK cell, and macrophage responses, ensuring immune tolerance during pregnancy.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
